16:["$","ul","b3175-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b3175",{"children":["Brand fidelity beats image quality. A beautiful asset that gets your palette wrong is a redo, not a shortcut."]}],["$","li","b3177",{"children":["Feed the tool your real brand inputs. A logo file, hex codes, and type rules fix drift that prompting alone won't."]}],["$","li","b3179",{"children":["Legible in-image text and photoreal material are won by different models, so expect to split a campaign across two."]}],["$","li","b3181",{"children":["A campaign isn't finished until it exists in every channel ratio, so weigh the resizing step as heavily as the generating step."]}]]}]
17:["$","h2","b3183",{"id":"what-separates-a-good-marketing-image-generator","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["What separates a good marketing image generator?"]}]
18:["$","p","b3185",{"children":["Four things, in rough order of how often they're the reason a tool gets abandoned after the first campaign."]}]
19:["$","h3","b3187",{"children":["Your brand survives the generation"]}]
1a:["$","p","b3189",{"children":["The failure everyone hits is an asset that's almost on brand. The palette drifts a shade, the logo gets redrawn as something logo-shaped, the type is a near-miss of your actual typeface. Look for somewhere to put the real inputs, a logo file and hex codes and type rules, instead of describing them in a prompt and hoping."]}]
1b:["$","h3","b3191",{"children":["Text that spells correctly"]}]
1c:["$","p","b3193",{"children":["Most marketing images carry words: an offer, a price, a tagline, packaging copy. Image models are still uneven here, and the gap between the best and the average is wide enough that it should drive which model runs which asset. Test your worst case, a long tagline in a specific typeface, not the word sale."]}]
1d:["$","h3","b3195",{"children":["Sets, not single assets"]}]
1e:["$","p","b3200",{"children":["Performance marketing runs on variants. If a tool makes one great image and then makes you start over for the next nineteen, it's a design tool rather than a marketing tool. The question is whether a working setup can be saved and re-run against new inputs, which is the same argument for a ",["$","$L5e","b3198",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b3197","href":"/blog/best-ai-creative-canvases-image-generation","isNewTab":false},"children":["node-based creative canvas"]}],"."]}]
1f:["$","h3","b3202",{"children":["Every ratio you actually ship"]}]
20:["$","p","b3204",{"children":["A square hero doesn't cover a story, a banner, and a paid social placement. Cropping a 1:1 to 9:16 loses the composition, so what you want is a tool that re-composes for the ratio instead of trimming it. This is the step teams most often forget to price in, and it's frequently more hours than the generating."]}]
21:["$","h2","b3206",{"id":"the-five-compared","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["The five compared"]}]
22:["$","div","b3207",{"role":"region","aria-label":"Comparison table, scroll horizontally to see all columns","tabIndex":0,"data-lenis-prevent":true,"className":"my-10 max-w-full overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-black/10 bg-white shadow-[0_1px_2px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-orange","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full min-w-[640px] border-collapse text-left","children":["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","b3208",{"className":"bg-black/[0.04]","children":[["$","td","b32080",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b3211",{"children":[["$","strong","b3210",{"children":["Tool"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b32081",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b3214",{"children":[["$","strong","b3213",{"children":["Where it fits"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b32082",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b3217",{"children":[["$","strong","b3216",{"children":["In-image text"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b32083",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b3220",{"children":[["$","strong","b3219",{"children":["Brand fidelity"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b32084",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b3223",{"children":[["$","strong","b3222",{"children":["Frontier output quality"]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b3224",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b32240",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3227",{"children":["Melius"]}]]}],["$","td","b32241",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3230",{"children":["Whole campaign, ideation through resizing"]}]]}],["$","td","b32242",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3233",{"children":["Routed to the model that handles type"]}]]}],["$","td","b32243",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3236",{"children":["5/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b32244",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3239",{"children":["5/5"]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b3240",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b32400",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3243",{"children":["Adobe Firefly"]}]]}],["$","td","b32401",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3246",{"children":["Brand-safe production inside Creative Cloud"]}]]}],["$","td","b32402",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3249",{"children":["Improving, not its strongest suit"]}]]}],["$","td","b32403",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3252",{"children":["4/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b32404",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3255",{"children":["3/5"]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b3256",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b32560",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3259",{"children":["Canva"]}]]}],["$","td","b32561",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3262",{"children":["Layout and finished collateral for a whole team"]}]]}],["$","td","b32562",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3265",{"children":["Handled in layout, not generated"]}]]}],["$","td","b32563",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":"$L5f"}],"$L60"]}],"$L61","$L62"]}]}]}]
23:["$","h2","b3305",{"id":"1-melius","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["1. Melius"]}]
24:["$","p","b3307",{"children":["Melius is the Agentic OS for creative work: you describe the campaign in plain language and an agent builds the workflow, picks the right model for each step, and leaves every step open for you to change. Underneath is a node-based canvas, so nothing is a black box, but many people who use Melius daily never need to open it."]}]
25:["$","p","b3309",{"children":["For marketing specifically, the useful part is that the whole job lives in one place. The brand inputs, the generation, the variants, and the channel resizing are steps in one graph instead of four tools with exports between them. Change the reference at the top and everything downstream re-runs."]}]
26:["$","h3","b3311",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
27:["$","ul","b3313-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b3313",{"children":["Brand anchor: your voice, palette, type and rules sit on the canvas as a reusable node you point at, not prompt text you retype."]}],["$","li","b3315",{"children":["Assets as inputs: a logo becomes its own node, and a product detail page URL can be scraped for real dimensions and materials."]}],["$","li","b3317",{"children":["Model routing per step, so the model that handles fabric isn't the one asked to set your tagline."]}],["$","li","b3319",{"children":["Magic resize re-composes an image for each aspect ratio instead of cropping it."]}],["$","li","b3321",{"children":["Documented recipes for the volume jobs: static ads from a reference style, scaling a winning ad into more variants, resizing for channels, and localizing."]}],["$","li","b3323",{"children":["Multiplayer, so a designer, a copywriter and a stakeholder can work and sign off on the same canvas."]}]]}]
28:["$","p","b3331",{"children":["The model routing is the part that changes how a campaign gets built. Melius publishes its own model-per-job guidance, and the split that matters for marketing is that style adherence, fabric and editorial lighting go to one model while legible typography and packaging copy go to another. On a single-model tool you pick one and accept the weaker half. Here the agent runs both inside one workflow, drawing on the ",["$","$L5e","b3326",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b3325","href":"/models","isNewTab":false},"children":["library of leading models"]}]," that comes with ",["$","$L5e","b3329",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b3328","href":"/blog/one-subscription-every-model","isNewTab":false},"children":["one subscription"]}],"."]}]
29:["$","p","b3333",{"children":["The catch: the agent has to be told what good looks like. Give it a vague brief and you get a vague campaign, and the brand anchor only helps if somebody sets it up properly first."]}]
2a:["$","p","b3335",{"children":["Best for: marketing teams and freelance creatives running repeat campaigns who want one place to go from brand inputs to every channel ratio."]}]
2b:["$","h2","b3337",{"id":"2-adobe-firefly","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["2. Adobe Firefly"]}]
2c:["$","p","b3339",{"children":["Firefly is the safe answer when the legal question comes before the creative one. Adobe trained it on licensed and public-domain material and offers enterprise customers indemnification, which for a regulated brand or a cautious legal team settles an argument no amount of output quality will."]}]
2d:["$","p","b3341",{"children":["It's also the only option here that sits natively inside the tools a large creative department already runs. Generated content moves into Photoshop, Illustrator and Express without an export step, and Firefly Boards covers the moodboard stage in the same account."]}]
2e:["$","h3","b3343",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
2f:["$","ul","b3345-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b3345",{"children":["Commercial safety as a product feature, with contractual IP indemnification available to enterprise customers as a purchasable entitlement covering select outputs."]}],["$","li","b3347",{"children":["Native round-tripping into Photoshop, Illustrator and Express."]}],["$","li","b3349",{"children":["Brand kits, so palette and type carry across generations."]}],["$","li","b3351",{"children":["Firefly Boards for the concepting stage, in the same subscription."]}],["$","li","b3353",{"children":["Generative fill and expand, which reviewers regularly rate best in class for extending an existing asset."]}]]}]
30:["$","p","b3355",{"children":["Firefly's weakness is the one its safety creates. A model trained on licensed stock tends toward the look of licensed stock, and marketers regularly report its output as more generic than what they get elsewhere. It's also the least flexible on model choice: you get Adobe's models, and when a better one ships somewhere else you wait."]}]
31:["$","p","b3357",{"children":["The catch: you're buying into the Adobe ecosystem, and the pricing only makes sense if you're already in it."]}]
32:["$","p","b3359",{"children":["Best for: brands and in-house teams where commercial safety and Creative Cloud integration outrank having the newest model."]}]
33:["$","h2","b3361",{"id":"3-canva","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["3. Canva"]}]
34:["$","p","b3363",{"children":["Canva is built to hand a non-designer a finished, on-brand asset. Its AI generation sits inside a layout tool that a whole marketing team already knows, so what comes out is the finished post and not an image you still have to place."]}]
35:["$","p","b3365",{"children":["Brand Kit is the underrated part for marketing. Fonts, colors and logos are locked at the account level, which means the intern's social graphic comes out on brand without anyone reviewing it."]}]
36:["$","h3","b3367",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
37:["$","ul","b3369-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b3369",{"children":["Generation inside a layout tool, so you get a finished asset, not raw imagery."]}],["$","li","b3371",{"children":["Brand Kit enforces fonts, colors and logos across everyone's work."]}],["$","li","b3373",{"children":["Bulk Create runs one design against a spreadsheet of copy, which covers a lot of variant work."]}],["$","li","b3375",{"children":["Resizing across channel formats is a first-class feature, not an afterthought."]}],["$","li","b3377",{"children":["The lowest training cost of anything here: most marketers already use it."]}]]}]
38:["$","p","b3379",{"children":["The ceiling is real, though. Canva's generative models lag the frontier, and for hero imagery, photoreal product work, or anything with an art-directed look, reviewers report the output shows it. Teams commonly generate elsewhere and lay out in Canva, which is a sensible split rather than a failure."]}]
39:["$","p","b3381",{"children":["The catch: the free plan's AI allowance is small enough that any real usage needs a paid seat, and the good generative features sit behind it."]}]
3a:["$","p","b3383",{"children":["Best for: small marketing teams and non-designers who need on-brand collateral out the door today."]}]
3b:["$","h2","b3385",{"id":"4-ideogram","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["4. Ideogram"]}]
3c:["$","p","b3387",{"children":["Ideogram exists because image models were bad at text, and it's still the tool most often named when the words in the image have to be right. If your asset is a promotional graphic, a poster, or packaging with real copy on it, this is the one to test first."]}]
3d:["$","p","b3389",{"children":["It's deliberately narrow, and that's the point. There's no brand system, no layout engine, and no campaign management. You describe an image with words in it and you get an image with the words spelled correctly."]}]
3e:["$","h3","b3391",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
3f:["$","ul","b3393-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b3393",{"children":["Legible, correctly spelled text inside generated images, more reliably than general-purpose models."]}],["$","li","b3395",{"children":["Magic Prompt expands a short brief into a fuller one, which helps typography come out styled instead of pasted on."]}],["$","li","b3397",{"children":["Style codes and reference images give you a repeatable look without training anything."]}],["$","li","b3399",{"children":["Free accounts get weekly credits if you sign in with Google, Apple or Microsoft, so you can test it against your real tagline before paying."]}],["$","li","b3401",{"children":["Fast enough to iterate on wording, which matters when the copy is the variable."]}]]}]
40:["$","p","b3403",{"children":["What you don't get is anything around the image. No brand kit to enforce, no variant pipeline, no channel resizing. It's a component in a marketing workflow rather than the workflow, which is exactly how most teams use it."]}]
41:["$","p","b3405",{"children":["The catch: it's a single-model tool, so everything outside its specialty is merely fine, and you'll be exporting to somewhere else to finish the job."]}]
42:["$","p","b3407",{"children":["Best for: anyone whose blocker is text rendering on one asset, not campaign volume."]}]
43:["$","h2","b3409",{"id":"5-pencil","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["5. Pencil"]}]
44:["$","p","b3411",{"children":["Pencil is built for one job at one scale: generating and testing large volumes of paid ad creative for brands that buy media seriously. It plugs into brand and product data and produces ads with performance prediction attached, which is a different proposition from the other four."]}]
45:["$","p","b3413",{"children":["It's here because at genuine enterprise volume that specialization pays. If you're running continuous creative testing across markets, a system designed around ad performance beats a general image generator."]}]
46:["$","h3","b3415",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
47:["$","ul","b3417-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b3417",{"children":["Ad-shaped output by default: formats, copy and layout aimed at paid placements."]}],["$","li","b3419",{"children":["Performance prediction on generated creative, so testing gets prioritized instead of being random."]}],["$","li","b3421",{"children":["Brand and product feed ingestion, which keeps claims and imagery consistent at volume."]}],["$","li","b3423",{"children":["Built for multi-market rollouts, including localized variants."]}],["$","li","b3425",{"children":["Enterprise onboarding, which for a large brand is a feature and not friction."]}]]}]
48:["$","p","b3427",{"children":["Pencil was acquired by The Brandtech Group in 2023 and has moved steadily toward enterprise since, so the self-serve path that smaller teams used to take is no longer the reliable way in. If you're a two-person marketing team, this is not your tool, and the other four all are."]}]
49:["$","p","b3429",{"children":["The catch: it's sales-led, so there's no way to try it this afternoon against your own assets."]}]
4a:["$","p","b3431",{"children":["Best for: brands with real media budgets running continuous creative testing across markets."]}]
4b:["$","h2","b3433",{"id":"running-a-campaign-on-melius","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Running a campaign on Melius"]}]
4c:["$","p","b3435",{"children":["Start with the brand anchor, because everything downstream inherits from it. Drop in your logo file, your hex codes and your type rules and it sits on the canvas as a node the rest of the graph points at, instead of prompt text somebody retypes each time."]}]
4d:["$","p","b3440",{"children":["Then start from a marketing template and let the agent route each step. Style adherence, material and editorial lighting go to one model; legible typography and packaging copy go to another, which is the split that decides whether an asset with words on it is usable. From one approved asset, the scaling recipe fires out the variant set, and magic resize re-composes each channel ratio instead of cropping it. The same shape works for ",["$","$L5e","b3438",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b3437","href":"/blog/best-ai-tools-product-photo-variants","isNewTab":false},"children":["product photo variants"]}],"."]}]
4e:["$","p","b3442",{"children":["Worth knowing where this stops: Melius gives you the imagery, not a laid-out post with your copy set in it. If what you need is the finished, scheduled thing, that still happens in a design tool."]}]
4f:["$","h2","b3444",{"id":"frequently-asked-questions","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Frequently asked questions"]}]
50:["$","div","b3445",{"className":"faq-list my-10 flex flex-col divide-y divide-black/10 border-y border-black/10","children":[["$","details","0",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["What is the best AI image generator for marketing?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"There isn't one that wins every stage, so match the tool to the job: Canva for finished on-brand collateral, Ideogram when the words in the image have to be right, Adobe Firefly when commercial safety and Creative Cloud integration matter most, and Melius when you want brand inputs, generation, variants and channel resizing to live in one re-runnable workflow. Pencil is the enterprise answer for high-volume paid testing."}]]}],["$","details","1",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Can AI image generators keep my brand consistent?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Yes, but only if you can give the tool your real brand inputs instead of describing them. Look for a brand kit, a brand anchor node, or an equivalent place to put a logo file, hex codes and type rules. Prompting a hex code is the approach that drifts, and it drifts worst across a large set."}]]}],["$","details","2",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Which AI model is best for text inside marketing images?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Text rendering is uneven across models, and it's worth splitting a campaign because of it. Melius publishes its own per-job guidance and routes legible typography and packaging copy to a different model than the one it uses for fabric, material and editorial lighting. Ideogram is the dedicated option if text is your only blocker."}]]}],["$","details","3",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Do I own the marketing images I generate?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":"$L63"}]]}],"$L64"]}],"$L65","$L66","$L67"]}]
51:["$","p","b3450",{"children":["Set your brand anchor once, then start from a marketing template and let an agent build the variant and resize steps around it. ",["$","$L5e","b3448",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b3447","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true},"children":["Open Melius"]}],"."]}]
52:["$","section","related",{"className":"relative w-full pb-section bg-gray-background","children":[["$","$L11",null,{"color":"gray"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"relative z-10 mx-auto w-full max-w-300 px-5 lg:px-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"t-h-2 mb-12 text-center text-balance text-gray-dark-1","children":"Related Articles"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto grid w-full max-w-max grid-cols-1 gap-11 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3","children":[["$","$L68","post-best-ai-tools-fashion-campaign-videos",{"post":{"_key":"post-best-ai-tools-fashion-campaign-videos","slug":"best-ai-tools-fashion-campaign-videos","category":"comparisons","title":"Best AI tools for creating fashion campaign videos","isoDate":"2026-09-06","date":"September 6, 2026","readTime":"11 Min Read","excerpt":"Five AI tools for fashion campaign video, compared on garment fidelity, holding one model across clips, fabric under light, and editorial motion.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/best-ai-tools-fashion-campaign-videos/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Melius Team"}],"faq":[{"question":"What is the best AI tool for fashion campaign videos?","answer":"It depends on whether the garment is real. For actual products you sell, a fashion-specific tool like WearView protects garment accuracy better than any general model. For brand campaign work with invented scenes, Runway gives the most cinematic control and Kling the most convincing human movement. Melius is the pick when you need a whole campaign set built once and re-run, because the look is agreed on a canvas and applied across every cut."},{"question":"Can AI keep the same model across a whole campaign?","answer":"Yes, if you use a reference or character mechanism instead of re-describing the person in each prompt. Description-based consistency drifts, and the drift shows up by the second or third clip. On Melius, references and character nodes are reused across every clip in the set, and Kling and Runway both support reference images for the same purpose."},{"question":"How long can an AI-generated fashion video be?","answer":"Most useful campaign output is 5 to 10 seconds per clip, and longer cuts are assembled from several generations, not produced in one pass. Plan the campaign as a set of short beats you edit together, because a single continuous 30 second generation is where garment and identity drift become obvious."},{"question":"Will AI video keep my garment accurate?","answer":"Not reliably, unless the tool is built for it. General video models treat your garment as a starting suggestion and will redesign necklines, seams, hardware and print placement, especially as the clip runs longer. Test the details that carry the garment's identity before committing, and if every item is a real SKU, weigh a fashion-specific tool over a general one."},{"question":"Do I own AI-generated fashion campaign videos?","answer":"It varies by tool, and it matters more here than in most categories because this output runs as paid media. On Melius you own what you create and can use it commercially, subject to the underlying model providers' terms, and Melius does not use your work to train AI models. WearView states commercial rights on its paid plans. Check each tool's own terms before a campaign goes live."},{"question":"Is AI fashion video cheaper than a video shoot?","answer":"For derivative work, substantially. For the hero asset, often not, once you count regenerations and the art direction time to get a usable take. The realistic economics are one real shoot plus AI for the variants, ratios, recolours and market cuts, which is where the volume of a fashion campaign actually sits."},{"question":"Do I need on-model photography to start?","answer":"No. Several tools generate from flat-lays or ghost mannequin shots, which is how e-commerce teams without a shoot budget get moving. Quality still tracks the input, so a sharp, evenly lit product shot produces a materially better clip than a phone snap."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"which-ai-tool-should-you-use-for-fashion-campaign-videos","title":"Which AI tool should you use for fashion campaign videos?"},{"_key":"what-to-know-before-you-pick","title":"What to know before you pick"},{"_key":"what-separates-a-good-fashion-video-tool","title":"What separates a good fashion video tool?"},{"_key":"the-five-compared","title":"The five compared"},{"_key":"1-melius","title":"1. Melius"},{"_key":"2-runway","title":"2. Runway"},{"_key":"3-higgsfield","title":"3. Higgsfield"},{"_key":"4-kling","title":"4. Kling"},{"_key":"5-wearview","title":"5. WearView"},{"_key":"building-a-campaign-set-on-melius","title":"Building a campaign set on Melius"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"Frequently asked questions"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3452","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3451","text":"Which AI tool should you use for fashion campaign videos?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"which-ai-tool-should-you-use-for-fashion-campaign-videos"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3454","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3453","text":"Start by deciding whether the garment in the video is a real product you sell, because that single fact splits these tools into two groups that are bad at each other's jobs. If it's a real product, garment fidelity governs and a fashion-specific tool saves you the fight. If the clothing is invented and the point is mood, a general video model gives you far more range.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3456","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3455","text":"The second thing worth knowing is that several of these tools run the same underlying models. What separates them is usually the workflow around the generation: how the garment gets held steady, how one look carries across clips, and what happens once the clip exists.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3458","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3457","text":"What to know before you pick","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-to-know-before-you-pick"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3460","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3459","text":"Real product or invented look? Garment fidelity and creative range pull against each other, and no tool here wins both.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3462","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3461","text":"Fabric is the tell. Drape, weight and sheen under moving light are what separate a campaign clip from an obvious generation.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3464","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3463","text":"Identity drift across clips ruins a set faster than any single clip's quality, so test the second and third clip, not the first.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3466","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3465","text":"Check commercial rights before anything runs as paid media, and check them per tool, because they differ.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3468","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3467","text":"What separates a good fashion video tool?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-separates-a-good-fashion-video-tool"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3470","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3469","text":"Four criteria, and the first one eliminates most general-purpose video models for real product work.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3472","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3471","text":"The garment stays the garment","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3474","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3473","text":"A generated clip that subtly redesigns your jacket is worse than useless, because it advertises something you don't sell. Watch the details that carry a garment's identity: the neckline, the seam lines, the hardware, the print placement. These are what drift first, and they drift more the longer the clip runs.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3476","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3475","text":"The same model across every clip","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3478","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3477","text":"A campaign is a set, and a set needs one person in it. Identity drift is the failure that makes an AI campaign read as AI, because a viewer notices the face changed between the story and the feed post even when they can't say why. Look for a reference or character mechanism instead of re-prompting a description each time.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3480","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3479","text":"Fabric under moving light","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3482","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3481","text":"Stills forgive material errors that motion exposes. Silk that doesn't catch light as it moves, denim with no weight, knitwear that behaves like plastic: all of it reads instantly to anyone who works in fashion. Test your hardest material, not a cotton t-shirt.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3484","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3483","text":"Motion that reads as editorial","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3486","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3485","text":"Fashion has its own camera language, and it's mostly restrained: a slow push, a locked-off frame, a single deliberate move. Tools that default to swooping drone energy produce something that looks like AI video rather than like a campaign. Control over the camera matters more here than in most categories.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3488","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3487","text":"The five compared","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"the-five-compared"},{"_type":"portableTable","_key":"b3489","rows":[{"_key":"b3490","cells":[{"_key":"b3491","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3493","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3492","text":"Tool","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b3494","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3496","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3495","text":"Best at","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b3497","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3499","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3498","text":"How it holds the garment","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b3500","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3502","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3501","text":"Consistency across clips","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b3503","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3505","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3504","text":"Free tier","marks":["strong"]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b3506","cells":[{"_key":"b3507","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3509","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3508","text":"Melius","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3510","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3512","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3511","text":"Building the whole campaign set in one workflow","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3513","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3515","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3514","text":"Your own stills as reference nodes, per-step model choice","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3516","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3518","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3517","text":"5/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3519","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3521","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3520","text":"Yes, limited trial credits, all models","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b3522","cells":[{"_key":"b3523","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3525","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3524","text":"Runway","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3526","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3528","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3527","text":"Cinematic control and in-house frontier models","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3529","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3531","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3530","text":"Image-to-video from your own frame","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3532","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3534","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3533","text":"4/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3535","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3537","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3536","text":"Yes, a one-time starting credit allowance","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b3538","cells":[{"_key":"b3539","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3541","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3540","text":"Higgsfield","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3542","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3544","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3543","text":"Camera moves and human motion","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3545","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3547","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3546","text":"Image-to-video with motion presets","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3548","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3550","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3549","text":"3/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3551","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3553","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3552","text":"Yes, watermarked, on limited models","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b3554","cells":[{"_key":"b3555","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3557","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3556","text":"Kling","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3558","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3560","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3559","text":"Realistic human movement, high resolution","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3561","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3563","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3562","text":"Image-to-video, strong on body mechanics","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3564","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3566","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3565","text":"3/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3567","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3569","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3568","text":"Yes, daily credits, but watermarked","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b3570","cells":[{"_key":"b3571","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3573","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3572","text":"WearView","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3574","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3576","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3575","text":"Real garments on real products","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3577","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3579","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3578","text":"Purpose-built for garment accuracy","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3580","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3582","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3581","text":"3/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3583","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3585","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3584","text":"Trial, commercial rights on paid plans","marks":[]}]}]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3587","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3586","text":"1. Melius","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"1-melius"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3589","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3588","text":"Melius is the Agentic OS for creative work: you describe the campaign and an agent builds the workflow, routes each step to the right model, and leaves every step editable. A node-based canvas sits underneath, so the whole pipeline from garment still to finished cut is visible and re-runnable, though plenty of people drive it from Slack and never open the canvas.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3591","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3590","text":"For fashion the advantage is that a campaign is a set of related outputs, and a canvas is the natural shape for that. One approved look feeds the hero cut, the social variants and the product page loop as branches of the same graph, not three separate jobs you do three times.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3593","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3592","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3595","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3594","text":"Two fashion templates ship in the product: fashion campaign video for an editorial look, and high-end fashion commercial for a studio scene built from model and garment photos.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3597","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3596","text":"Fabric and texture analysis reads an input garment and writes the expert prompt for manipulating it, which is the step most people get wrong by hand.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3599","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3598","text":"Per-step model routing, so the model that renders fabric isn't the one asked to carry the motion.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3601","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3600","text":"References and character nodes carry one look across every clip in the set.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3603","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3602","text":"Storyboard turns a single image into a 9-panel sequence, which is a fast way to agree a campaign's shape before generating video.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3605","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3604","text":"Multiplayer, so the art director and the producer work on the same canvas instead of trading exports.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3610","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b3607","href":"/models","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3606","text":"The model routing is what makes this practical rather than theoretical. Melius publishes its own per-job guidance and it splits fashion work across models deliberately: material, fabric and editorial lighting go to one, faces and character consistency to another, cinematic motion to a third. Because the whole ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3608","text":"library of leading models","marks":["b3607"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3609","text":" sits on one subscription, the agent can use all three inside a single workflow instead of making you pick a favourite and live with its weak side.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3612","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3611","text":"The catch: this is a workflow tool, so the first campaign takes longer to set up than typing a prompt into a single-model app. The payoff arrives on the second campaign, when the graph is already built.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3614","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3613","text":"Best for: brands and agencies producing a campaign set, not one clip, who want the look agreed once and then applied across every cut.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3616","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3615","text":"2. Runway","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"2-runway"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3618","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3617","text":"Runway's approach has been to build its own frontier video models instead of reselling everyone else's. Its Gen-4 line is exclusive to the platform, which is the strongest single argument for paying for it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3620","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3619","text":"It's also the most film-literate tool here. The controls assume you know what a camera does, and the output rewards that knowledge, which suits fashion work more than the consumer-shaped alternatives.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3622","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3621","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3624","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3623","text":"In-house frontier models you can't get anywhere else, alongside access to several third-party models on one plan.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3626","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3625","text":"Genuine camera and motion control, not a preset menu.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3628","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3627","text":"Strong image-to-video, which is how most fashion campaign work actually starts.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3630","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3629","text":"A mature editing surface around the generation, so clips get assembled and not merely produced.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3632","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3631","text":"Long-established use in professional film and advertising work, which makes craft knowledge easy to find.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3634","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3633","text":"Credits go fast at the good settings, and the frontier model is the expensive one, so users report a real campaign on Runway costing more than the headline plan price suggests. It also gives you no help with garment accuracy specifically: it's a general video model, and it will happily redesign your jacket while making a beautiful clip.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3636","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3635","text":"The catch: budget by the clip rather than by the month, and expect to regenerate.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3638","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3637","text":"Best for: teams with film instincts who want maximum control and are willing to pay for the frontier model.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3640","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3639","text":"3. Higgsfield","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"3-higgsfield"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3642","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3641","text":"Higgsfield's angle is motion, specifically camera motion. Where most tools ask you to describe a shot, Higgsfield gives you named moves to apply to a still, which turns out to be a fast and reliable way to get a clip that looks directed instead of drifting.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3647","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b3644","href":"/blog/higgsfield-alternative","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3643","text":"For fashion that's more useful than it sounds. A locked-off frame with one deliberate push is most of what campaign video needs, and getting there by picking a move beats getting there by prompt archaeology. We've written separately on ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3645","text":"Higgsfield alternatives","marks":["b3644"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3646","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3649","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3648","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3651","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3650","text":"Named camera moves applied to a still, which is the fastest route to a directed-looking clip.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3653","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3652","text":"Human motion and fabric behaviour, which Higgsfield attributes to a team background in computer vision and biomechanics.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3655","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3654","text":"A low entry price relative to the frontier platforms.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3657","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3656","text":"Quick iteration, so testing several moves on one garment still is cheap.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3659","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3658","text":"Good results from a single input image, with no reference set required.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3661","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3660","text":"The preset approach is also the ceiling. Once you want a move that isn't in the menu, or a longer cut with more than one beat, you're working against the tool. Consistency holds reasonably well inside one preset and slips when you mix them across a campaign set.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3663","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3662","text":"The catch: it's a clip generator, not a campaign system, so assembly and versioning happen somewhere else.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3665","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3664","text":"Best for: getting a good-looking single clip out of a strong still, quickly and cheaply.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3667","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3666","text":"4. Kling","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"4-kling"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3669","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3668","text":"Kling is the pick when a person has to move convincingly. Its handling of body mechanics, weight and gait is among the best available, and it holds up at higher resolutions than most of the field, which matters if the clip is going anywhere bigger than a phone.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3671","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3670","text":"It shows up in fashion work often for exactly that reason. A walk that reads as a real walk is most of a campaign clip's credibility.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3673","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3672","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3675","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3674","text":"Realistic human movement, above all walking and full-body motion.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3677","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3676","text":"High output resolution relative to the category.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3679","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3678","text":"Solid image-to-video from a single model shot.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3681","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3680","text":"Reference support for holding a subject across clips.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3683","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3682","text":"Available on several platforms besides its own, including Melius.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3685","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3684","text":"The tooling around Kling is thinner than the model deserves. There's no brand system, no campaign structure, and the interface assumes you're making one clip at a time. It's also the entry where checking which version you're actually getting matters most, because platforms reselling it don't all expose the same one.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3687","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3686","text":"The catch: a strong model with light workflow around it, so plan on assembling the campaign elsewhere.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3689","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3688","text":"Best for: clips where the model's movement is the thing the viewer will judge.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3691","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3690","text":"5. WearView","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"5-wearview"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3693","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3692","text":"WearView is the specialist, and on its own narrow job it beats every general tool here. It's built for fashion e-commerce: virtual try-on, AI model creation, ghost mannequin work, and short fashion video generated from the product shots you already have.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3695","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3694","text":"The reason to consider it over anything else on this list is garment accuracy. Its own documentation describes animating flat-lays, ghost mannequins and model shots while holding the same model and the same garment across clips, which is precisely the problem general video models don't solve.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3697","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3696","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3699","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3698","text":"Purpose-built for real garments, so the clothing is treated as a fixed input, not something to reinterpret.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3701","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3700","text":"Movement templates such as a catwalk walk or a 360 degree spin, which covers most product-page video needs.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3703","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3702","text":"Ghost mannequin and flat-lay inputs, meaning you don't need on-model photography to start.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3705","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3704","text":"Same model and garment held across a set of clips, per its documentation.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3707","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3706","text":"Commercial usage rights on paid plans, which its own pages state plainly.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3709","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3708","text":"The narrowness cuts both ways. For a brand campaign with invented scenes, art-directed lighting and a mood that isn't a product spin, WearView has far less range than any of the general models, and you'll hit its edges quickly. It's also a much smaller company than the rest of this list, which is worth weighing if this becomes core infrastructure.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3711","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3710","text":"The catch: excellent inside e-commerce fashion video, limited outside it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3713","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3712","text":"Best for: fashion e-commerce teams animating real SKUs for product pages and paid social.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3715","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3714","text":"Building a campaign set on Melius","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"building-a-campaign-set-on-melius"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3717","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3716","text":"Begin with one good garment still and the fashion campaign video template for an editorial look, or high-end fashion commercial if you're building a studio scene from model and garment photos. Run fabric and texture analysis on the input first: it writes the prompt for handling that specific garment, which is the step most people get wrong by hand.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3725","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b3719","href":"/blog/brief-to-execution-workflow","isNewTab":false},{"_type":"link","_key":"b3722","href":"/blog/best-ai-image-generators-marketing","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3718","text":"Hold the look with references and character nodes rather than re-describing the model each time, because description-based consistency drifts by the second or third clip. The agent splits the work across models deliberately, sending fabric and editorial lighting one way, faces and character consistency another, and cinematic motion a third. Storyboard turns a single frame into a 9-panel sequence, which is the cheapest way to agree a campaign's shape before you generate any video. The same ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3720","text":"brief-to-execution workflow","marks":["b3719"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3721","text":" applies to the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3723","text":"marketing image side of a campaign","marks":["b3722"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3724","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3727","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3726","text":"The honest limit is long takes. Flowing fabric across 20 continuous seconds, or hands touching clothing, is still where a real shoot is cheaper than the retries.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3729","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3728","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b3730","items":"$52:props:children:1:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:post:faq"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3735","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b3732","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3731","text":"Start from the fashion campaign video template with one garment still, then branch it into the ratios and cuts your channels need. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3733","text":"Open Melius","marks":["b3732"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3734","text":".","marks":[]}]}]}}],"$L69","$L6a"]}]]}]]}]
