60:["$","td","b32564",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3271",{"children":["2/5"]}]]}]
61:["$","tr","b3272",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b32720",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3275",{"children":["Ideogram"]}]]}],["$","td","b32721",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3278",{"children":["Single assets where the words must be right"]}]]}],["$","td","b32722",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3281",{"children":["Its whole reason for existing"]}]]}],["$","td","b32723",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3284",{"children":["2/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b32724",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3287",{"children":["3/5"]}]]}]]}]
62:["$","tr","b3288",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b32880",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3291",{"children":["Pencil"]}]]}],["$","td","b32881",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3294",{"children":["High-volume paid ad creative for brands"]}]]}],["$","td","b32882",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3297",{"children":["Built around ad copy and layout"]}]]}],["$","td","b32883",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3300",{"children":["3/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b32884",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3303",{"children":["2/5"]}]]}]]}]
63:["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]
64:["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"It varies by tool, so check before anything runs as paid media. On Melius you own what you create and can use it commercially, subject to the underlying model providers' terms, and Melius does not use your work to train AI models. Adobe makes contractual IP indemnification available to enterprise customers as a purchasable entitlement covering select Firefly outputs, which is the strongest position here if legal review is your constraint."}]
65:["$","details","4",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Is there a free way to generate marketing images?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Yes, and it's enough to evaluate with, though not to run a campaign on. Melius is free to sign up with limited trial credits and access to all models, Ideogram gives eligible free accounts weekly credits, and Canva and Firefly both include small monthly AI credit allowances on their free plans. Check each tool's own pricing page, because these allowances change often."}]]}]
66:["$","details","5",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["How many variants do I actually need?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Enough to test a real hypothesis, which in paid social usually means tens, not hundreds. The number matters less than whether your setup can produce the next batch without being rebuilt, so judge a tool on whether a working configuration is saved and re-runnable against new inputs."}]]}]
67:["$","details","6",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Can AI replace a designer on marketing work?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"No, and the tools that work best are the ones that assume it won't. The taste, the brief and the final call stay with a person; what these tools remove is the repetitive production work around the decision, like resizing an approved asset into fourteen placements. That's the part that was never the creative part."}]]}]
69:["$","$L68","post-best-tools-ai-generated-design-concepts",{"post":{"_key":"post-best-tools-ai-generated-design-concepts","slug":"best-tools-ai-generated-design-concepts","category":"comparisons","title":"Best tools for AI generated design concepts","isoDate":"2026-09-05","date":"September 5, 2026","readTime":"10 Min Read","excerpt":"Five AI tools for generating design concepts, compared on how precisely you can set a direction, comparing options, and reusing a look later.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/best-tools-ai-generated-design-concepts/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Melius Team"}],"faq":[{"question":"What is the best AI tool for design concepts?","answer":"Match it to the discipline: Midjourney for the loosest visual exploration, Vizcom for physical product concepts from sketches, Recraft for identity and vector systems, and Melius when the approved direction has to be reapplied across a body of work. Kosmik is the one to add if your problem is research and not generation."},{"question":"Can AI generate design concepts that are actually usable?","answer":"Yes at the direction stage, less so as finished work. These tools are strong at proposing and resolving a look and weak at the precision a production asset needs, so the realistic use is to settle the direction with AI and finish in your normal tools. Treat the output as a concept, which is what it's good at."},{"question":"How do I keep a concept consistent once it's approved?","answer":"Capture the direction as something reusable instead of one image. A written style description, a saved style, or a brand kit can all be reapplied months later; a single lucky generation cannot. On Melius the approved direction stays as a node you re-run against new inputs, which is the same idea made concrete."},{"question":"Is Midjourney still the best for concept art?","answer":"For range and aesthetic quality it's still the one most designers reach for first, and style references have made it much more directable. Its weaknesses are everything after the idea: brand control, legible text, exact palettes and getting a look out of Midjourney and into real assets. There's also no free tier, so you can't test it against your references before paying."},{"question":"Do I need to be able to draw to use AI concepting tools?","answer":"No for graphic and brand concepting, and it helps a lot for product concepting. Vizcom is built around a sketch and rewards being able to make one, while the others take a written direction or a reference set. If you can't draw, working from references instead of from a blank prompt gets you much closer."},{"question":"Do I own concepts I generate with AI?","answer":"It varies by tool, so check before a concept goes into client work. On Melius you own what you create and can use it commercially, subject to the underlying model providers' terms, and Melius does not use your work to train AI models. Read the terms per tool, because free consumer tiers are the ones most likely to restrict commercial use."},{"question":"Will AI concepting replace art direction?","answer":"No. Generating options is now nearly free, which makes choosing between them the scarce skill and no longer the easy part. The judgment about which direction is right for this brand and this audience is the work, and these tools remove the labour around that decision, not the decision itself."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"which-ai-tool-should-you-use-for-design-concepts","title":"Which AI tool should you use for design concepts?"},{"_key":"what-to-know-before-you-pick","title":"What to know before you pick"},{"_key":"what-separates-a-good-concepting-tool","title":"What separates a good concepting tool?"},{"_key":"the-five-compared","title":"The five compared"},{"_key":"1-melius","title":"1. Melius"},{"_key":"2-midjourney","title":"2. Midjourney"},{"_key":"3-vizcom","title":"3. Vizcom"},{"_key":"4-recraft","title":"4. Recraft"},{"_key":"5-kosmik","title":"5. Kosmik"},{"_key":"from-approved-concept-to-finished-asset","title":"From approved concept to finished asset"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"Frequently asked questions"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3737","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3736","text":"Which AI tool should you use for design concepts?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"which-ai-tool-should-you-use-for-design-concepts"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3739","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3738","text":"Choose based on what you're concepting, because the tools that win product design and the tools that win brand direction are barely in the same category. A physical product needs a sketch turned into something buildable. A campaign direction needs a look you can defend in a room and then reproduce. Those are different problems.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3741","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3740","text":"The trap in this category is judging tools on whether the output is beautiful. At the concept stage beauty is cheap and abundant. What's scarce is a direction specific enough to brief against, and a look that survives when you apply it to the next twelve assets.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3743","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3742","text":"What to know before you pick","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-to-know-before-you-pick"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3745","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3744","text":"Concepting and rendering are separate jobs. Exploring twenty directions and resolving one of them reward different tools.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3747","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3746","text":"A direction you can write down is worth more than one you stumbled into, because only the written one is briefable.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3749","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3748","text":"You'll generate far more than you present, so how fast you can compare and discard matters as much as output quality.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3751","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3750","text":"Check whether the concept can travel. A look trapped in one tool's session is a look you'll rebuild later.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3753","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3752","text":"What separates a good concepting tool?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-separates-a-good-concepting-tool"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3755","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3754","text":"Four things, and the last one is the one people discover too late.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3757","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3756","text":"How precisely you can set a direction","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3759","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3758","text":"There's a wide gap between picking minimal from a menu and specifying a warm neutral palette, soft top light from camera-left, matte ceramic surfaces and a shallow depth of field. The second is what lets you match an existing brand or an art director's reference. Judge a tool on how much of that it will actually listen to.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3761","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3760","text":"Comparing directions side by side","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3766","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b3763","href":"/blog/best-ai-creative-canvases-image-generation","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3762","text":"Concepting is divergent by nature: you make five directions to kill four. A tool that shows you one output at a time forces you to hold the comparison in your head, which is where good options get lost. Being able to branch a direction and see the alternatives together is worth more than a marginally better single image, which is the argument for a ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3764","text":"node-based creative canvas","marks":["b3763"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3765","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3768","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3767","text":"Whether the look survives to the next asset","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3770","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3769","text":"A concept's job is to be applied. If the approved direction exists only as one lucky image, somebody has to reverse-engineer it for every asset that follows. A look captured as a reusable style, a written description or a saved configuration is one you can still apply in three months.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3772","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3771","text":"Getting to something you can present","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3774","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3773","text":"Concepts get shown to people who didn't make them, which means a raw generation is rarely the deliverable. Mockups, placements, a board that reads as considered: the tools differ a lot on how much of that they'll do, and it's usually the difference between a concept being approved and being misunderstood.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3776","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3775","text":"The five compared","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"the-five-compared"},{"_type":"portableTable","_key":"b3777","rows":[{"_key":"b3778","cells":[{"_key":"b3779","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3781","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3780","text":"Tool","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b3782","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3784","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3783","text":"Concepting it suits","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b3785","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3787","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3786","text":"How you set a direction","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b3788","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3790","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3789","text":"Reusable afterwards","marks":["strong"]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b3791","cells":[{"_key":"b3792","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3794","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3793","text":"Melius","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3795","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3797","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3796","text":"Brand, campaign and asset direction","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3798","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3800","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3799","text":"Style analysed from a reference, or written out","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3801","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3803","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3802","text":"Yes, as a node you re-run","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b3804","cells":[{"_key":"b3805","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3807","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3806","text":"Midjourney","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3808","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3810","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3809","text":"Mood, visual exploration, concept art","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3811","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3813","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3812","text":"Style references and moodboards","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3814","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3816","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3815","text":"Partly, via style references","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b3817","cells":[{"_key":"b3818","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3820","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3819","text":"Vizcom","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3821","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3823","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3822","text":"Physical product and industrial design","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3824","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3826","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3825","text":"Your own sketch, plus material prompts","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3827","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3829","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3828","text":"Yes, models carry into computer-aided design","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b3830","cells":[{"_key":"b3831","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3833","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3832","text":"Recraft","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3834","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3836","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3835","text":"Brand identity, icons and vector systems","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3837","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3839","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3838","text":"Brand kits and style presets","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3840","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3842","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3841","text":"Yes, styles are saved and reapplied","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b3843","cells":[{"_key":"b3844","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3846","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3845","text":"Kosmik","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3847","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3849","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3848","text":"Visual research before you generate anything","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3850","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3852","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3851","text":"You collect it, and it surfaces adjacents","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3853","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3855","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3854","text":"Yes, the board is the artefact","marks":[]}]}]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3857","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3856","text":"1. Melius","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"1-melius"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3859","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3858","text":"Melius is the Agentic OS for creative work: describe the direction you're chasing and an agent builds the workflow, picks the right model per step, and leaves every step editable. A node-based canvas underneath turns a concept into a graph you can branch, compare and re-run.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3861","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3860","text":"That shape suits concepting unusually well. Five directions become five branches off one reference instead of five separate sessions, and the one that gets approved is already a working configuration you point at the next asset.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3863","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3862","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3865","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3864","text":"Image style analysis reads a reference image and describes its style, which turns somebody's moodboard into something briefable.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3867","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3866","text":"Sketch to image resolves a rough drawing into realistic detail, so a napkin idea becomes presentable without redrawing it.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3869","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3868","text":"Brand anchor holds palette, type and rules as a node, so concepts stay inside the brand instead of drifting out of it.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3871","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3870","text":"Branching on the canvas puts competing directions side by side instead of one after another.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3873","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3872","text":"Storyboard turns a single image into a 9-panel sequence, which is a quick way to show a direction as a narrative.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3875","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3874","text":"Multiplayer, so the review happens on the work, not in a separate thread of screenshots.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3880","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b3877","href":"/models","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3876","text":"The style-analysis step is the one that changes the work. Most concepting dies at the handoff, where an approved image has to become a brief that somebody else can execute against. Reading the style out of the reference as text closes that gap: the direction becomes words you can argue with, edit and reapply, not a vibe attached to one file. Behind it sits a ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3878","text":"library of leading models","marks":["b3877"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3879","text":", so the model that analyses a reference isn't the one asked to render the concept.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3882","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3881","text":"The catch: the payoff is in the reuse, so for a single one-off concept you'll feel the setup cost without collecting the benefit.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3884","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3883","text":"Best for: brand and campaign concepting where the approved direction has to be applied across a body of work.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3886","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3885","text":"2. Midjourney","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"2-midjourney"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3888","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3887","text":"Midjourney is still the default for visual exploration, and among art directors and brand designers it's the one that gets opened first. Its output has a point of view, which sounds like a criticism and is actually the reason it works for concepting: it proposes things you wouldn't have asked for.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3890","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3889","text":"Style references and moodboards have made it considerably more directable than it used to be. You can hand it a set of images and get work in that register, which is the mechanism most concepting workflows now hang off.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3892","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3891","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3894","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3893","text":"An aesthetic range that proposes directions you would not have thought to specify.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3896","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3895","text":"Style references let you steer toward an existing look without training anything.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3898","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3897","text":"Moodboards build a persistent personal aesthetic you can generate against.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3900","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3899","text":"Genuinely fast divergent exploration, which is the core concepting motion.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3902","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3901","text":"A very large community, so the craft knowledge is easy to find.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3904","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3903","text":"It remains weak at everything after the idea. Precise brand control, legible text, exact palettes and structured output are all outside what it's trying to do, and there's no free tier to test it against your own references first. Concepts also tend to stay in Midjourney: getting an approved look applied to real assets means rebuilding it somewhere else.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3906","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3905","text":"The catch: unmatched at proposing directions, unhelpful at executing them.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3908","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3907","text":"Best for: the earliest, loosest stage, when you want range rather than control.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3910","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3909","text":"3. Vizcom","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"3-vizcom"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3912","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3911","text":"Vizcom is the tool here built for physical products, and if that's what you design it's not really competing with the rest of the list. It takes an industrial designer's sketch and renders it, keeping the geometry you drew instead of reinterpreting it into something merely similar.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3914","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3913","text":"The reason it matters is that product concepting has a downstream that graphics work doesn't. A concept has to become a model somebody engineers, and Vizcom sends work toward computer-aided design instead of stopping at a pretty picture.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3916","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3915","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3918","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3917","text":"Sketch to render that respects your linework instead of redrawing it.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3920","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3919","text":"Material and finish exploration on a fixed form, which is exactly how product concepting iterates.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3922","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3921","text":"3D output, with a path into Autodesk Fusion for the engineering handoff.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3924","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3923","text":"Adaptive Canvas removes fixed aspect-ratio limits mid-project.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3926","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3925","text":"Unify composites a design into a real environment with matched lighting, for validation shots.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3928","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3927","text":"Outside physical product design it's the wrong tool, and it doesn't pretend otherwise. There's no brand system, no campaign thinking, and no reason to reach for it if your concepts are graphics, layouts or campaign imagery. Its pricing has also moved around, so check its own pricing page rather than a third-party tracker.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3930","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3929","text":"The catch: superb at one discipline, irrelevant to the others.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3932","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3931","text":"Best for: industrial, product and packaging designers working from sketches toward something manufacturable.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3934","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3933","text":"4. Recraft","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"4-recraft"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3936","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3935","text":"Recraft performs best when the concept has to be a design system, not an image. It generates true vectors, editable in Illustrator or Figma, which means a logo or icon concept arrives as something a designer can actually finish, not a raster to trace.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3938","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3937","text":"For brand concepting the brand kit is the useful mechanism. Colours, style preferences and identity parameters are stored and applied across everything you generate, so a set of concepts holds together instead of each one being its own accident.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3940","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3939","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3942","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3941","text":"True scalable vector graphics output, editable downstream in standard design tools.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3944","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3943","text":"Brand kits that carry colour and identity parameters across a whole set of concepts.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3946","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3945","text":"Style presets you can define once and reapply, which keeps a system coherent.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3948","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3947","text":"Strong at icons, illustration and the flat graphic work most AI tools handle badly.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3950","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3949","text":"A low paid entry point relative to what it does.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3952","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3951","text":"It's narrower than it looks. Photoreal imagery, campaign scenes and anything cinematic are not what Recraft is for, and reviewers rate its raster output as unremarkable next to the frontier models. Treat it as the vector and identity specialist, not a general concepting tool.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3954","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3953","text":"The catch: brilliant inside vector and brand-system work, ordinary outside it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3956","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3955","text":"Best for: identity, icon and illustration concepts that need to survive into production files.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3958","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3957","text":"5. Kosmik","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"5-kosmik"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3960","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3959","text":"Kosmik is on this list as the honest counterweight: it generates nothing. It's a spatial canvas for visual research, where you collect images, PDFs, video and live web pages, and it surfaces related material and organises what you've gathered.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3962","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3961","text":"It earns the slot because a lot of what people call concepting is really research, and doing that badly is why generated concepts come out generic. Feeding a model a considered reference set produces better work than feeding it a sentence, and this is a tool for building the reference set.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3964","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3963","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3966","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3965","text":"An infinite spatial canvas that holds mixed media, including live web pages, in one place.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3968","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3967","text":"Surfaces related visual material from something you've uploaded, so research compounds.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3970","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3969","text":"Auto-organises a growing reference library instead of leaving you to file it.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3972","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3971","text":"The board itself is the deliverable, which suits a direction review well.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3974","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3973","text":"A 1-week free trial, enough to build a first board and see whether the habit sticks.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3976","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3975","text":"If you need an image made, this is not the tool, and pairing it with a generator is the actual workflow. It's also a smaller product than the rest of this list, which matters if it becomes where your reference library lives.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3978","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3977","text":"The catch: it improves the input to concepting rather than doing the concepting.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3980","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3979","text":"Best for: art directors and brand designers whose reference libraries have outgrown a folder of screenshots.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3982","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3981","text":"From approved concept to finished asset","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"from-approved-concept-to-finished-asset"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3984","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3983","text":"The handoff is where concepting work usually leaks, and it's worth planning for before you start, not after a direction is signed off.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3986","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3985","text":"The failure looks like this: a concept gets approved as a single image, the person who made it moves on, and everyone downstream reverse-engineers the look from that one file. Palette drifts, the type is a near-miss, and three assets in, nobody can say what the direction actually was. The concept was never written down, so it couldn't be applied.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3991","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b3988","href":"/blog/best-ai-image-generators-marketing","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3987","text":"Avoiding it is mostly a matter of capturing the direction as something other than an image: a written style description, a saved style, a brand kit, a configuration you can re-run. Tools differ on whether they let you do that, and it's the criterion that separates a concepting tool from a nice image generator. If a look can only exist as one output, treat the concept as unfinished. The same discipline is what makes ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3989","text":"marketing image generation","marks":["b3988"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3990","text":" survive past the first asset.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3993","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3992","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b3994","items":"$69:props:post:faq"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3999","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b3996","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3995","text":"Drop a reference image on the canvas, run image style analysis to turn it into a written direction, then branch it into the concepts you want to compare. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3997","text":"Open Melius","marks":["b3996"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3998","text":".","marks":[]}]}]}}]
6a:["$","$L68","post-best-ai-creative-canvases-image-generation",{"post":{"_key":"post-best-ai-creative-canvases-image-generation","slug":"best-ai-creative-canvases-image-generation","category":"comparisons","title":"Best AI creative canvases for image generation","isoDate":"2026-09-05","date":"September 5, 2026","readTime":"12 Min Read","excerpt":"Five AI creative canvases compared on who builds the graph, which models you can reach, whether workflows are reusable, and how they price collaboration.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/best-ai-creative-canvases-image-generation/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Melius Team"}],"faq":[{"question":"What is an AI creative canvas?","answer":"It's a workspace where creative work is built as a graph rather than typed into a single prompt box: each prompt, image, video or edit is a node, and edges pass one node's output into the next. That structure means a multi-step pipeline lives visually in one place, and you can change an early step and re-run everything after it instead of starting again."},{"question":"What is a node-based AI canvas?","answer":"A node-based canvas represents each creative step as a node you connect to others, so the whole pipeline is visible and editable. The advantage over a chat interface is that the process is kept, not lost: you can rewire a step, branch to compare two directions, or reuse a working graph as a template for the next job."},{"question":"Do I have to learn node graphs to use one?","answer":"Not on all of them. Krea, Flora, Figma Weave and ComfyUI all expect you to build the graph yourself, with ComfyUI asking the most. On Melius an agent builds and runs the graph from a plain-language description and leaves it there for you to inspect, so the node interface is available, not required."},{"question":"Is ComfyUI still worth learning in 2026?","answer":"Yes, if you want total control and are willing to maintain it. Its flexibility and its price are hard to argue with, and the community ecosystem around it is deep. The reason most creatives don't is the time cost: you become responsible for models, dependencies and hardware, and none of that is the creative work."},{"question":"Which AI canvas gives access to the most models?","answer":"ComfyUI, in absolute terms, because you can install anything, including models no commercial platform hosts. Among hosted tools, the ones spanning image, video and audio across several providers on one subscription give the widest practical reach, and Melius keeps a live registry of what it currently supports. Model libraries change monthly, so check the current list instead of trusting a comparison post."},{"question":"How much does an AI creative canvas cost?","answer":"ComfyUI is free if you self-host. Among the paid tools, free plans exist across the board but are small, and the number that matters more than the headline price is how seats are charged: Flora prices per seat, Figma Weave's Team plan per user, and Melius includes up to 8 seats on self-serve plans and unlimited seats on Enterprise. Check each pricing page, because these change often."},{"question":"Can several people work on the same canvas?","answer":"On some of them, and it's worth checking what it costs. Real multiplayer means a designer, a copywriter and a reviewer can all be in the same document while it's being built, which is the main argument for a canvas over individual tools. ComfyUI has effectively none, and the commercial tools differ mainly in whether collaboration is priced per head."},{"question":"Do I own what I make on a creative canvas?","answer":"Usually, but confirm it per tool. On Melius you own what you create and can use it commercially, subject to the underlying model providers' terms, and Melius does not use your work to train AI models. Figma Weave includes a commercial license even on its free plan. Self-hosted ComfyUI leaves the question to the licences of whichever models you install."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"what-is-the-best-ai-creative-canvas-for-image-generation","title":"What is the best AI creative canvas for image generation?"},{"_key":"what-to-know-before-you-pick","title":"What to know before you pick"},{"_key":"what-separates-a-good-ai-canvas","title":"What separates a good AI canvas?"},{"_key":"the-five-compared","title":"The five compared"},{"_key":"1-melius","title":"1. Melius"},{"_key":"2-krea","title":"2. Krea"},{"_key":"3-flora","title":"3. Flora"},{"_key":"4-figma-weave","title":"4. Figma Weave"},{"_key":"5-comfyui","title":"5. ComfyUI"},{"_key":"when-you-don-t-need-a-canvas-at-all","title":"When you don't need a canvas at all"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"Frequently asked questions"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2887","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2886","text":"What is the best AI creative canvas for image generation?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-is-the-best-ai-creative-canvas-for-image-generation"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2889","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2888","text":"The right canvas is the one whose graph you won't have to build by hand, because on every tool here the graph is the product and the only real difference is who assembles it. A canvas beats a prompt box for anything with more than one step, since each prompt, image and edit becomes a node you can rewire and re-run instead of starting over. That part is settled.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2891","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2890","text":"What isn't settled is the cost of entry. Node tools have historically asked you to learn them first, which is a fine trade for a technical artist and a bad one for a creative director who just wants the work made. That's the axis these five separate on.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2893","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2892","text":"Each entry says where something else is the better choice, and pricing links out to each tool's own page.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2895","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2894","text":"What to know before you pick","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-to-know-before-you-pick"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2897","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2896","text":"The canvas is the substrate, not the selling point. Ask who builds the graph, because that's what you're actually choosing between.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2899","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2898","text":"Model breadth decides your ceiling. A canvas wired to one vendor's models inherits that vendor's weak spots.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2901","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2900","text":"A graph you can save and re-run is the whole return on learning one of these, so check what reuse looks like before committing.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2903","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2902","text":"Read the seat pricing carefully. Several of these charge per person, and a canvas that nobody else can open loses most of its point.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2905","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2904","text":"What separates a good AI canvas?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-separates-a-good-ai-canvas"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2907","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2906","text":"Four criteria, and the first is the one that decides whether the tool gets used after week two.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2909","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2908","text":"Whether you have to learn it","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2911","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2910","text":"Node graphs are a real interface with real concepts, and most creatives have no interest in acquiring them. The question is whether the tool expects you to wire nodes yourself, or whether something else does that from a plain description while leaving the graph there for you to inspect. Both are valid; they suit different people.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2913","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2912","text":"Which models you can reach","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2915","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2914","text":"The point of a canvas is combining steps, and steps are better when each can use the best model for its job. Material and fabric, legible type, faces, motion: these are won by different models, and a canvas limited to one family forces a compromise at every step. Check how the library is kept current, too, because this field moves monthly.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2917","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2916","text":"Whether the graph is reusable","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2919","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2918","text":"Building a working pipeline is an investment, and it only pays back if you can point it at new inputs next week. Look for templates, saved workflows, or an equivalent, and check whether a saved graph accepts fresh inputs or has to be edited in place each time.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2921","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2920","text":"Whether other people can work on it","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2923","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2922","text":"Creative work is reviewed, and review that happens on the canvas beats review that happens in a thread of exported screenshots. Multiplayer matters, and so does what it costs: a tool priced per seat quietly discourages the collaboration it advertises.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2925","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2924","text":"The five compared","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"the-five-compared"},{"_type":"portableTable","_key":"b2926","rows":[{"_key":"b2927","cells":[{"_key":"b2928","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2930","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2929","text":"Tool","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b2931","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2933","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2932","text":"Who builds the graph","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b2934","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2936","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2935","text":"Ease of use","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b2937","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2939","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2938","text":"Model choice","marks":["strong"]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b2940","cells":[{"_key":"b2941","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2943","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2942","text":"Melius","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2944","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2946","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2945","text":"An agent, from a plain-language brief","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2947","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2949","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2948","text":"5/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2950","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2952","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2951","text":"Image, video and audio across many providers","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b2953","cells":[{"_key":"b2954","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2956","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2955","text":"Krea","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2957","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2959","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2958","text":"You do, on a suite rather than a node graph","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2960","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2962","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2961","text":"4/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2963","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2965","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2964","text":"Wide, with its own real-time and upscale models","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b2966","cells":[{"_key":"b2967","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2969","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2968","text":"Flora","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2970","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2972","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2971","text":"You do, with Flows to structure it","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2973","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2975","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2974","text":"3/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2976","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2978","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2977","text":"Image, video and text","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b2979","cells":[{"_key":"b2980","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2982","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2981","text":"Figma Weave","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2983","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2985","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2984","text":"You do, wiring nodes by hand","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2986","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2988","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2987","text":"2/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2989","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2991","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2990","text":"All its supported image models on every plan","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b2992","cells":[{"_key":"b2993","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2995","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2994","text":"ComfyUI","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2996","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2998","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2997","text":"You do, from the primitives up","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2999","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3001","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3000","text":"1/5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3002","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3004","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3003","text":"Anything you can install or host","marks":[]}]}]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3006","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3005","text":"1. Melius","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"1-melius"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3008","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3007","text":"Melius is the Agentic OS for creative work, and the first node-based canvas made for agents. You describe the work in plain language, Mel, the Melius agent, wires the graph, routes each node to the right model and runs it, and every prompt and step stays open for you to change. The canvas is there when you want it and ignorable when you don't, which is the whole design.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3010","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3009","text":"It's also the only one here you can drive from outside the app. Slack, an application programming interface (API), a command-line interface (CLI), and Model Context Protocol (MCP) all act on the same canvas, so the work can start wherever you already are.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3012","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3011","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3014","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3013","text":"An agent builds and runs the graph from a description, so the node interface is optional, not a prerequisite.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3016","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3015","text":"One subscription spanning image, video and audio models from several providers, with per-step routing.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3018","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3017","text":"Templates ship in the product, covering the common jobs, and a working graph can be reused as one.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3020","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3019","text":"Multiplayer with multiple people and multiple agents on one canvas at the same time, and up to 8 seats on self-serve plans and unlimited seats on Enterprise.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3022","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3021","text":"Search with AI on the Professional plan, so generations and uploads stay searchable instead of getting lost.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3024","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3023","text":"Nothing is a black box: change an early node and everything downstream re-runs.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3032","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b3026","href":"/pricing","isNewTab":false},{"_type":"link","_key":"b3029","href":"/models","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3025","text":"The seat pricing is the underrated part. Every other tool on this list either charges per person or assumes one, and a canvas is a collaboration surface, so paying per head to let a stakeholder look at the work cuts against the reason you bought it. Self-serve plans include up to 8 seats for your team and reviewers, with unlimited seats on Enterprise. Plans start at $18 a month as of August 2026, current pricing is on the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3027","text":"pricing page","marks":["b3026"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3028","text":", and the current library of leading models is listed on the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3030","text":"models page","marks":["b3029"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3031","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3034","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3033","text":"The catch: an agent is only as good as the brief. A vague description produces a vague graph, and you'll still want to look at the canvas when the output isn't what you meant.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3036","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3035","text":"Best for: creative teams who want the benefits of a node pipeline without anyone having to become a node person.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3038","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3037","text":"2. Krea","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"2-krea"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3040","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3039","text":"Krea is a fast way to explore, and it gets there by not being a node graph. It's a creative suite with a canvas surface, built around real-time generation where the image updates as you move things, which is a genuinely different feel from prompt-and-wait.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3042","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3041","text":"The breadth is the other draw. Image, video, 3D, real-time, upscaling and its own fine-tuning all sit in one subscription, with a large model library and a very large style catalogue behind a deliberately spare interface.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3044","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3043","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3046","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3045","text":"Real-time generation, which makes exploration feel like sketching rather than querying.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3048","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3047","text":"A wide model library plus its own models, including upscaling to very large output sizes.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3050","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3049","text":"Training your own style, so a look becomes reproducible without prompt archaeology.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3052","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3051","text":"A clean interface that hides most of the complexity, which suits solo work.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3054","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3053","text":"A daily free allowance of 100 compute units, enough to evaluate it properly.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3056","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3055","text":"Because it isn't node-based, multi-step pipelines are weaker here. There's no real equivalent of a saved graph you point at new inputs, so repeatable production work means repeating yourself. Collaboration is thin too: this is a tool built around one person exploring quickly.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3058","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3057","text":"The catch: superb for exploration, structurally unsuited to a workflow you run every week.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3060","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3059","text":"Best for: solo creatives and designers who want speed and range over repeatability.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3062","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3061","text":"3. Flora","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"3-flora"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3064","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3063","text":"Flora is a genuine node canvas with a narrative bent. Its Flows feature structures a graph along a story arc, which makes it a natural fit for storyboarding, sequences and anything where the output is a series, not a single asset.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3066","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3065","text":"Of the hand-wired canvases here it's the friendliest. The interface is designed for creatives, not engineers, and the concepts arrive gradually enough that a designer can get productive without a tutorial marathon.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3068","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3067","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3070","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3069","text":"Flows structure a workflow along a narrative arc, which suits storyboards and sequences.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3072","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3071","text":"A node canvas designed for creatives, with a gentler learning curve than the engineering-first tools.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3074","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3073","text":"Image, video and text nodes in one graph.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3076","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3075","text":"Genuinely pleasant to use, which matters more than it sounds for adoption.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3078","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3077","text":"A free plan to try it, though a small one.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3083","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b3080","href":"/blog/flora-alternative","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3079","text":"The free tier is the tightest on this list, capped at a small lifetime allowance instead of a monthly one, so evaluating it properly means paying. Pricing is per seat, which adds up quickly for a team, and you still build every graph yourself. There's a fuller side-by-side in our ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3081","text":"Flora alternative piece","marks":["b3080"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3082","text":" if you're weighing the two directly.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3085","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3084","text":"The catch: you're still the one wiring it, and the seat pricing punishes collaboration.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3087","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3086","text":"Best for: creatives working on sequences and narrative-shaped output who want a canvas that doesn't feel like software.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3089","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3088","text":"4. Figma Weave","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"4-figma-weave"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3091","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3090","text":"Figma Weave is the node canvas with the strongest institutional backing. Formerly Weavy, it was acquired by Figma in October 2025, and it chains image, video, 3D and editing steps as nodes you connect and run.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3093","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3092","text":"Its real advantage is where it sits. If your team already works in Figma, having generation adjacent to design files removes an export step and a lot of context switching, and that convenience beats a better model most days.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3095","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3094","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3097","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3096","text":"A proper node canvas for chaining generation and editing steps.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3099","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3098","text":"Full access to all its supported AI image models on every plan, including the free one.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3101","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3100","text":"A commercial license included on the free plan, which is unusually generous.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3103","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3102","text":"Figma's backing, which is the strongest signal here that the tool will still exist in three years.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3105","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3104","text":"Adjacency to design files for teams already standardised on Figma.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3110","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b3107","href":"/blog/figma-weave-alternative","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3106","text":"You wire everything by hand, and the free plan's 5 workflows and 150 monthly credits go quickly once you're doing real work. The Team plan is priced per user, so a canvas a whole team can open is the expensive configuration. Our ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3108","text":"Figma Weave alternative piece","marks":["b3107"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3109","text":" covers the comparison in more detail.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3112","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3111","text":"The catch: excellent if you live in Figma, and a hand-built graph either way.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3114","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3113","text":"Best for: design teams already standardised on Figma who want generation in the same neighbourhood.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3116","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3115","text":"5. ComfyUI","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"5-comfyui"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3118","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3117","text":"ComfyUI is where this whole category started, and it's free. It's open source with well over a hundred thousand stars on GitHub, it runs on your own hardware, and it will run models no hosted tool exposes.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3120","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3119","text":"For a technical artist who wants that level of control, it's still the right trade. Total control over every model, parameter and output, no per-generation billing, and no vendor deciding which models you're allowed to reach.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3122","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3121","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3124","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3123","text":"Complete control over every model, parameter and step in the pipeline.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3126","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3125","text":"Free and open source, self-hosted on your own graphics processing unit (GPU), with no usage metering.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3128","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3127","text":"Any model you can install, including ones no commercial platform hosts.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3130","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3129","text":"An enormous ecosystem of community nodes and shared workflows.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3132","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3131","text":"Comfy Cloud for a hosted option if you'd rather not run the hardware.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3134","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3133","text":"The cost is time, and it's substantial. You manage models, dependencies and hardware, and the learning curve is the steepest here by a wide margin. Collaboration is barely there, and a graph that works on your machine is not automatically a graph that works on a colleague's. This is exactly the trade Melius is built to avoid: the canvas is the right infrastructure, and most creatives shouldn't have to learn it to benefit from it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3136","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3135","text":"The catch: unlimited capability in exchange for becoming the person who maintains it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3138","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3137","text":"Best for: technical artists and engineers who want control and have the patience the tool demands.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3140","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3139","text":"When you don't need a canvas at all","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"when-you-don-t-need-a-canvas-at-all"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3142","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3141","text":"A canvas is overhead, and for a decent share of creative work the overhead isn't worth it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3144","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3143","text":"If your job is one image from one prompt, a single-model tool is faster and you should use one. If it's a finished, laid-out social post, a design tool with templates will get you there sooner. If it's a one-off you'll never repeat, the investment in building a graph has nothing to pay back. The canvas earns its keep at the point where a job has several steps and you'll run something like it again, which is when starting over each time becomes the expensive option.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3149","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b3146","href":"/blog/agentic-image-generation-tools-compared","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3145","text":"The other honest limit is that a canvas doesn't improve the models. Every tool here draws on broadly the same frontier models, so a canvas won't make a weak generation good. What it changes is how much of your work survives: the process is kept, inspectable and re-runnable, instead of disappearing into a chat thread you can't reconstruct next month. Who assembles that graph is a separate question, covered in our comparison of ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3147","text":"agentic image generation tools","marks":["b3146"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3148","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3151","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3150","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b3152","items":"$6a:props:post:faq"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3157","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b3154","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3153","text":"Describe the pipeline you want in plain language and let an agent wire the graph, then open the canvas only if you want to change how it works. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3155","text":"Open Melius","marks":["b3154"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3156","text":".","marks":[]}]}]}}]
